text:
marta: seeing occasional "Unexpected end of JSON input" in our Node sample app when consuming SSE. Repro when user tab times out or when auth rotates mid-stream. sample-app uses node 18 + @redwood/sdk-js. anyone else?

liam: yes. I can repro by forcing a short client timeout (close stream) while a large `data:` event is mid-flight. Node's handler does JSON.parse per event and fails if the event is split across TCP chunks.

vikas: can you paste a tiny repro? This sounds like the \"tail buffer across reconnects\" gap we discussed. /cc @tori for runtime rotate behavior.

marta: minimal snippet (naive):
```js
res.on('data', chunk => {
  const parts = chunk.toString().split('\n\n');
  parts.forEach(p => {
    if (p.startsWith('data: ')) JSON.parse(p.slice(6)); // throws on split
  });
});
```
error: `SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input`

liam: workaround: keep a tail buffer and only parse when you see the SSE delimiter. preserve that tail across reconnects. e.g.: `let tail=''; tail += chunk; while (tail.indexOf('\n\n')>-1){...}`. Also try/catch JSON.parse and requeue raw if it fails.

vikas: action: I'll add a small persistent tail buffer to node SDK and unit tests that simulate: client abort mid-event, forced auth rotate, and proxy re-chunking. Also add telemetry `sse_parse_error` and optional `strict_seq` mode when server supplies seq numbers.

tori: runtime note: when we rotate auth we sometimes tear down and re-open streams. We can emit an optional `event: control` pre-rotate with `{"type":"pre_rotate","last_seq": <n>}` and the new stream can emit `{"type":"resume","last_seq": <n>}` so clients can reconcile. For forced 401s we'll try to include resume info on the new stream.

marta: I'll update the onboarding quickstart and sample-app README with the robust parsing pattern, mention token TTL as a short-term mitigation, and link to the SDK issue.

ci-bot: Created issue #4810: "sdk-js(node): SSE partial-chunk parse errors on client timeout/auth rotate - add tail buffer & seq handling" assigned to vikas.

vikas: plan: land buffer + tests tomorrow, enable telemetry flag for SRE, then add optional seq gap detection. will ping when PR is up.

marta: thanks ":thumbsup:" — will hold off on ramping sample-app until patch lands and then smoke test.
